{"author_count":3,"contributors":["Johansen, Ask Greve","Jensen, Jens Stissing","Galland, Daniel"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-823190"],"filters":{"added":"2025-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"urban experimentation and bureaucratic urban politics in planning for urban sustainability","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-823190","ids":["aau-12e56cd7-a41c-4ceb-b58d-2b20c19789ca"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Local-1-1-87BB2E21297868FCE8E943DA103C7AB0"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Sustainability and Planning"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Ask Greve","key":"johansenpau","last":"Johansen","locid":"c228bd62-c057-4f0a-9017-b44b88e449dc","name":"Johansen, Ask Greve","orcid":"0000-0002-4619-7940","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jens","key":"iuelstissingpau","last":"Iuel-Stissing","locid":"75cb3a27-7322-4fe9-bbf3-c815190a05bf","name":"Jensen, Jens Stissing","name_org":"Iuel-Stissing, Jens","orcid":"0000-0003-3535-3773","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Daniel","key":"gallandpau","last":"Galland","locid":"3107d24f-dd75-4a43-8868-fd812d352b44","name":"Galland, Daniel","orcid":"0000-0003-2648-806X","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.4337/9781035347483.00022","pages":"187-199","publisher":"Edward Elgar Publishing","status":"p","title":"Planning for Urban Sustainability: Doctrines, Disciplines, and Practices"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-12e56cd7-a41c-4ceb-b58d-2b20c19789ca"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Urban experimentation and bureaucratic urban politics in planning for urban sustainability","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-823190","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"The relationship between the market and the state in energy transitions is a popular contemporary topic. While some argue that the role of the state is mainly to fix market failures, research on state entrepreneurialism contends that states should engage in energy transitions by shaping markets to support societal objectives. This study contributes to this debate by examining how the Danish state has engaged in developing specific low-carbon energy resource economies, informed by different versions of economizations (i.e. specific bureaucratic ways of understanding and intervening in the economy and the markets pertaining to a resource). This study demonstrates that the Danish state’s engagement in biogas development from a local energy resource to biomethane that is suited for European gas markets has been contingent on shifting biogas economizations. We identify the pivotal moment when a sequence of political agreements marked intensified state support of biogas, including a taskforce organized in the Danish Energy Agency (2012–2016). We conceptualize this as a shift towards an entrepreneurial version of economization seeking to actively promote biogas investments and demonstrate how this version of economization was cultivated in parallel to a dominant bureaucratic version of economization with a mode of reasoning that adhered to socio-economic cost efficiency. We argue that states are likely to be characterized by a bureaucratic repertoire of economizations that can coexist, albeit with tensions between them, with relative significance that may shift over time. These dynamics are likely to shape states’ engagement in cultivating economies for low carbon energy resources.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Holm Jacobsen, Peter","Johansen, Ask Greve","Iuel-Stissing, Jens"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-827208"],"filters":{"added":"2025-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Holm Jacobsen, Peter"],"keyword":["Biogas","Energy transitions","State entrepreneurialism","Versions of economization"],"level":"sci","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-CBS"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-CBS"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"from efficiency to state entrepreneurialism shifting versions of the economization of biogas in the danish state","src":["cbs"],"src-code":["DI-U-CBS"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-827208","identifier":[{"id":"105012732194","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["cbs-f146e98f-15ce-40fb-a0f6-3b3f8ede0023"],"keyword":["Biogas","Energy transitions","State entrepreneurialism","Versions of economization"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-A4EE5513CC876FC3F0AABC69395E90D7"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"cbs copenhagen business school","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-CBS","l3nl":"Copenhagen Business School","l3nn":"CBS Copenhagen Business School","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"CBS Copenhagen Business School","namevar":["Copenhagen Business School, Department of Organization"],"nora_code":"DI-U-CBS","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Peter","key":"holmjacobsenpau","last":"Holm Jacobsen","locid":"c1257737-a4c5-4f2d-84d3-53feecb4208a","name":"Holm Jacobsen, Peter","orcid":"0000-0002-8538-7691","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Ask Greve","key":"johansenpau","last":"Johansen","name":"Johansen, Ask Greve","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Jens","key":"iuelstissingpau","last":"Iuel-Stissing","name":"Iuel-Stissing, Jens","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1177/0308518x251358606","issn":["0308518X","14723409"],"issn_org":["0308518X"],"journal":"Environment and Planning A","publisher":"SAGE Publications","status":"p","title":"Environment and Planning A","title_org":"Environment and Planning A: Economy and Space"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-105012732194"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","Copenhagen Business School","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["cbs-f146e98f-15ce-40fb-a0f6-3b3f8ede0023"],"src":["CBS Copenhagen Business School"],"title":"From Efficiency to State Entrepreneurialism : Shifting Versions of the Economization of Biogas in the Danish State","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-827208","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"The development of non-fossil energy resources has become a critical component of contemporary energy transition governance. We argue that some of the dominant governance models supporting the development of new energy resources are informed by a continuity-biased understanding of how the generation of new resources is likely to occur. In contrast, this paper suggests that new energy resources may develop through discontinuities. Based on a case study of resource-making activities pertaining to biogas in Denmark, we argue that the integration of new knowledge within established resource configurations can provoke disruptive reconfigurations. Empirically, our study demonstrates how biogas was initially configured as a local heating resource informed by farmers’ knowledge concerning operation of biogas reactors in the 1970s. From 2005 to 2012 biogas was reconfigured as biomethane with relevance to the low-carbon transition of the national energy system, informed by energy system knowledge that addressed it as a mess of molecules. Finally, from 2012 to 2016 biomethane was rendered into an attractive object of capital investment by reconfiguring green biomethane as a virtual green market object. Our findings suggest that knowledge that redefines and re-organises the configuration of energy resources is an important aspect of low-carbon transition governance.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Jensen, Jens Stissing","Jacobsen, Peter Holm","Johansen, Ask Greve"],"cuid":["S02-093.41-792961"],"filters":{"added":"2025-04","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Iuel-Stissing, Jens","Jensen, Jens Stissing"],"keyword":["Knowledge","Resource making","Shifting biogas configurations","Transition governance"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci","soc"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-CBS"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-CBS"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"governing resource making in energy transitions a study of shifting configurations of biogas in denmark from farming to big business","src":["aau","cbs"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-CBS"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1080/1523908X.2025.2451701","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["This work was supported by Independent Research Fund Denmark [grant number 0217-00422B]."],"id":"S02-093.41-792961","identifier":[{"id":"85215125934","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-9557468c-2063-4e81-a254-5aec6a403c2c","cbs-78644ab0-4929-4924-824f-198229255c00"],"keyword":["Resource making","knowledge","shifting biogas configurations","transition governance"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology","Social Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-8EDF1B3770DDD5140D29281B83F2D00E"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://research-api.cbs.dk/ws/files/112130182/Governing_resource_making_in_energy_transitions_a_study_of_shifting_configurations_of_biogas_in_Denmark_from_farming_to_big_business.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1080/1523908X.2025.2451701","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Sustainability and Planning","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Sustainability and Planning, Center for Design, Innovation and Sustainable Transitions","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Sustainability and Planning, Planning for Urban Sustainability"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"cbs copenhagen business school","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-CBS","l3nl":"Copenhagen Business School","l3nn":"CBS Copenhagen Business School","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"CBS Copenhagen Business School","namevar":["Copenhagen Business School, Department of Organization"],"nora_code":"DI-U-CBS","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jens","key":"luelstissingpau","last":"Luel-Stissing","locid":"75cb3a27-7322-4fe9-bbf3-c815190a05bf","name":"Jensen, Jens Stissing","name_org":"Luel-Stissing, Jens","orcid":"0000-0003-3535-3773","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Peter","key":"holmjacobsenpau","last":"Holm Jacobsen","locid":"c1257737-a4c5-4f2d-84d3-53feecb4208a","name":"Holm Jacobsen, Peter","orcid":"0000-0002-8538-7691","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Ask","key":"grevejohansenpau","last":"Greve Johansen","locid":"c228bd62-c057-4f0a-9017-b44b88e449dc","name":"Johansen, Ask Greve","name_org":"Greve Johansen, Ask","orcid":"0000-0002-4619-7940","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1080/1523908x.2025.2451701","issn":["15227200","1523908X"],"issn_org":["1523908X"],"issue":"4","journal":"Journal of Environmental Policy and Planning","pages":"362-375","publisher":"Routledge","status":"p","title":"Journal of Environmental Policy and Planning","volume":"27"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85215125934"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","Copenhagen Business School","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-9557468c-2063-4e81-a254-5aec6a403c2c","cbs-78644ab0-4929-4924-824f-198229255c00"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","CBS Copenhagen Business School"],"title":"Governing Resource Making in Energy Transitions : A Study of Shifting Configurations of Biogas in Denmark from Farming to Big Business","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-093.41-792961","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"This chapter considers how the notion of care makes specific scholarly accounts of bureaucracy possible. Knowledges and worlds produced within bureaucratic settings has often played the role of a ‘hegemonic’ backdrop against which alternative knowledges, attachments, politics have been put to the fore. Recounting an ethnographic engagement with a strategic urban planning office in Copenhagen, I highlight how the initial framing of the research collaboration, which entailed researching and developing liveability assessment tools in the municipality, gave cause for several instances of me being troubled by the expected outcome of my research. A careful engagement with these troubles both gives pause in ways that are worth considering and carries a potential to transform the situation from where the researcher intervenes. Being troubled both by the likely political consequences of building tools for liveability governance, and the immediately apparent possible ways of relating as researcher to this unease, I suggest that rethinking the notion of the useful idiot, and acting as one, became a viable response to these troubles. Furthermore, I suggest that the notion of care may be useful not only in terms of engaging with (hegemonic) power, but also as a means to reveal how exercised power itself may be vulnerable and undervalued as a caring practice.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Johansen, Ask Greve"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-673703"],"filters":{"added":"2023-07","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["CARE","Intervention","Liveability","Strategic urban planning"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"caring for the bureaucracy","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"http://www.scopus.com/inward/record.url?scp=85202004507&partnerID=8YFLogxK","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-673703","identifier":[{"id":"85202004507","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-62bbda27-509c-4347-9fbc-49fc513dc534"],"keyword":["care","idiocy","intervention","liveability","strategic urban planning"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-5E3291ED04C9C2CA971DC7B04DD8B835"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Sustainability and Planning","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Sustainability and Planning, SUSTAINABLE DESIGN AND TRANSITION"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Ask Greve","key":"johansenpau","last":"Johansen","locid":"c228bd62-c057-4f0a-9017-b44b88e449dc","name":"Johansen, Ask Greve","orcid":"0000-0002-4619-7940","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Doris","key":"lydahlpedh","last":"Lydahl","name":"Lydahl, Doris","rank":2,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Niels Christian Mossfeldt","key":"nickelsenpedh","last":"Nickelsen","name":"Nickelsen, Niels Christian Mossfeldt","rank":3,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/978-3-031-44119-6_15","edition":"1","eisbn":["9783031441196"],"isbn":["9783031441189"],"pages":"225-239","publisher":"Springer","status":"p","subtitle":"Careful Engagements in Healthcare, Museums, Design and Beyond","title":"Ethical and Methodological Dilemmas in Social Science Interventions"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85202004507"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-62bbda27-509c-4347-9fbc-49fc513dc534"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Caring for the Bureaucracy","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-673703","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
