Planning, Center for Design, Innovation and Sustainable Transitions","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Sustainability and Planning, Planning for Urban Sustainability"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anne","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","name":"Jensen, Anne","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jens","key":"iuelstissingpau","last":"Iuel-Stissing","locid":"75cb3a27-7322-4fe9-bbf3-c815190a05bf","name":"Jensen, Jens Stissing","name_org":"Iuel-Stissing, Jens","orcid":"0000-0003-3535-3773","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Morten","key":"ellepau","last":"Elle","locid":"f889442d-1bd0-4635-9a08-16e3eaef2ccf","name":"Elle, Morten","orcid":"0000-0002-2808-1012","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Ask Greve","key":"johansenpau","last":"Johansen","locid":"c228bd62-c057-4f0a-9017-b44b88e449dc","name":"Johansen, Ask Greve","orcid":"0000-0002-4619-7940","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"pages":"52","status":"p"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-c6830b24-59d4-407e-aae6-32a78ab7c134"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Sol Over Byen - Energifællesskaber mellem strategi, metagovernance og praksis","type":"Report","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-107671","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"In the Technical and Environmental Administration of the City of Copenhagen (TEA), strategic urban planners ponder how to value liveability in ways that align with the administration's political priorities. The elusive notion of liveability (what is it, exactly?) is interesting to explore – not as a solution, but as a problem to the situated practice of strategic urban planning. This PhD thesis investigates liveability as a problem and the related practice of operationalising it for bureaucratic practice. The basis for this investigation is participant observation of strategic urban planning in the TEA from 2017 to 2020, as well as ethnographic reading of documents collected through the research process. The core of the thesis is structured in three parts. In the first, the relation between measuring liveability and strategic planning is conceptualised through a reading of a diverse literature on liveability. Then I proceed to outline how a post-ANT approach can assist in thinking of strategic urban planning, specifying how a general underdetermination of the nature of the social can be explored empirically through attention to the composition of common worlds and the material-semiotics of the office setting from which the planner works. The second part engages with terms of participation in TEA, which not only hosted but also funded the research for the PhD thesis. Through the notion of situated intervention, I position the thesis research alongside and in curious conversation with TEA practice. I cultivate a methodological attention to the messiness of planning practice and slipperiness of agency with a baroque understanding of the research field. The third main part reconstructs the empirical work as four planning stories, recounting my discovery of the importance of opaqueness in strategic planning, a staged intervention in urban planning work in the TEA, the emergence of the surprisingly green Local Authority Plan for Copenhagen 2019, and lastly, how urban nature is made governable by number work with and by planner's tools. The thesis describes the construction of ways of knowing and valuing liveability, not as a comprehensive whole, but as dispersed and tangentially related assemblages. These constructions represent the urban territory in different ways and make their representations tangible as planners’ tools. Planners’ tools both reveal and conceal, interchangeably or simultaneously. The skilled planner works the space between revealing and concealing when crafting tangibility in strategic planning practice.","author_count":1,"contributors":["Johansen, Ask Greve"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-822310"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"1 contributor","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"und","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"opaqueness and tangibility a post ant account of the operationalisation of liveability in strategic planning the city of copenhagen 000000002017 000000002020","src":["aau","itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ITU"],"type":"doi","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/713716635/PHD_AGJ.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-822310","ids":["aau-519f9f60-3f78-4bd8-b169-f7d83dd9b40d","itu-9b49f91f-554c-4d07-9727-3f0eed2ada9b"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-2-9B0FC7603C19FD01C17C54FFAC742439"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/713716635/PHD_AGJ.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/files/713716635/PHD_AGJ.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Sustainability and Planning","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Sustainability and Planning, Planning for Urban Sustainability","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Sustainability and Planning, SUSTAINABLE DESIGN AND TRANSITION"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Ask Greve","key":"johansenpau","last":"Johansen","locid":"c228bd62-c057-4f0a-9017-b44b88e449dc","name":"Johansen, Ask Greve","orcid":"0000-0002-4619-7940","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["24461628"],"pages":"243","publisher":"Aalborg Universitetsforlag","series":"Ph.d.-serien for Det Tekniske Fakultet for IT og Design, Aalborg Universitet","status":"p"},"review":"Undetermined","search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-519f9f60-3f78-4bd8-b169-f7d83dd9b40d","itu-9b49f91f-554c-4d07-9727-3f0eed2ada9b"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Opaqueness and Tangibility : A post-ANT account of the operationalisation of liveability in strategic planning. The city of Copenhagen, 2017-2020","type":"Other-Internet Publication","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-822310","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"This chapter describes how staging human and non-human actors can help sort and articulate attachments in a setting characterized by an abundance of normativities. Utilizing the notions of situated intervention and environmental theatre, we describe uncertain and shifting actor positions as the City of Copenhagen attempted to implement a strategy for urban nature. This process entailed a re-evaluation of what ‘nature’ might be in an urban setting and how people and government entities should relate to it. We describe an intervention whereby the staging process was used as a tool for (re)problematization in collaboration with involved actors. The process revealed that narrating stories to connect bureaucratic practice with concern for urban nature was more important than developing stronger management tools to account for urban nature, thereby revealing what was specifically problematic in the practice.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Johansen, Ask Greve","Lindegaard, Hanne"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-088764"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Actor network theory","Multiplicity","Public administration","Situated Intervention","Staging","Urban nature"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"storytelling urban nature situated intervention as environmental theatre","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-088764","identifier":[{"id":"85137423425","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-84fe032f-699e-4ea1-813f-5f9f90c71859"],"keyword":["Actor-Network Theory","multiplicity","public administration","situated intervention","staging","urban nature"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-FB5630B0FD54B95713B94360B18728E2"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Sustainability and Planning","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Sustainability and Planning, SUSTAINABLE DESIGN AND TRANSITION"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Ask Greve","key":"johansenpau","last":"Johansen","locid":"c228bd62-c057-4f0a-9017-b44b88e449dc","name":"Johansen, Ask Greve","orcid":"0000-0002-4619-7940","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Hanne","key":"lindegaardpau","last":"Lindegaard","locid":"9b5a07ad-c191-4fdb-9c60-5d39675f4f76","name":"Lindegaard, Hanne","orcid":"0000-0003-3709-869X","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Christian","key":"clausenpedh","last":"Clausen","name":"Clausen, Christian","rank":3,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Dominique","key":"vinckpedh","last":"Vinck","name":"Vinck, Dominique","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Signe","key":"pedersenpedh","last":"Pedersen","name":"Pedersen, Signe","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Jens","key":"dorlandpedh","last":"Dorland","name":"Dorland, Jens","rank":6,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.4337/9781839103438.00025","eisbn":["9781839103438"],"isbn":["9781839103421"],"pages":"200-214","publisher":"Edward Elgar Publishing","status":"p","subtitle":"An Action-Oriented Participatory Approach","title":"Staging Collaborative Design and Innovation"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoI